# Local developer infrastructure: self-service, scoped, fail-closed

Follow root AGENTS.md and the current [owned developer environments runbook](../../docs/runbooks/dev-worktree-stacks.md) when a runtime is actually needed. Verify current commands, actual acceptance state and assigned worktree/environment identity; use only its normal start/status/stop path. Do not substitute release, another slot, Compose or static snapshot for missing dev capability. Explicit context; never ambient kubectl.

Local failure diagnosis is scoped to owned resources, not global reset authority. Preserve foreign workloads, reservations, credentials and SQL/S3/Temporal tenants. On failed admission or startup park only own attempted workloads under current runbook. Stop on ownership/UID/port/process conflict, unverified lease, unsafe admission, paid calls, protected mutation or architecture contradiction. No blanket tilt down, kind delete, reset or PID-only kill.
